---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="gl1tch — your AI, your terminal, your rules">

<main>

<!-- ── Hero ──────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="hero" id="hero">
<div class="hero-wrap">
  <div class="hero-left">
    <h1 class="hero-title">gl1tch</h1>
    <p class="hero-tagline">Shell does the work.<br>LLM does the thinking.<br>You own the workflow.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <pre class="code copyable hero-cmd" data-copy="brew install 8op-org/tap/glitch"><span class="p">$</span> brew install 8op-org/tap/glitch</pre>
      <div class="hero-links">
        <a href="https://github.com/8op-org/gl1tch" class="btn btn-primary">GitHub</a>
        <a href="/docs/getting-started" class="btn btn-ghost">Docs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-right">
    <pre class="code hero-demo"><span class="r">;; agentic mode — LLM pulls its own context</span>

(<span class="k">workflow</span> <span class="s">"pr-review"</span>

  (<span class="k">step</span> <span class="s">"fetch"</span>
    (<span class="k">sh</span> <span class="s">"gh pr view ~input --json title,body,files"</span>))

  (<span class="k">step</span> <span class="s">"review"</span>
    (<span class="k">llm</span> <span class="r">:agentic</span> <span class="s">true</span> <span class="r">:max-rounds</span> <span class="s">10</span>
      <span class="r">:prompt</span> <span class="s">```
        PR: ~(ref "fetch")
        Read the changed files.
        Review as a senior engineer.
        ```</span>)))</pre>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- ── What it does ─────────────────────────── -->
<section id="features">
<div class="wrap-wide">
  <div class="section-label">what you get</div>

  <div class="features-grid">

    <div class="feature-card feature-hero-card">
      <div class="feature-number">01</div>
      <h3>Agentic LLM steps</h3>
      <p>Set <code>:agentic true</code> and the LLM loops — calling tools, reading files, grepping code — until it has everything it needs. No more pre-stuffing prompts with context.</p>
      <pre class="code feature-code">(<span class="k">llm</span> <span class="r">:agentic</span> <span class="s">true</span> <span class="r">:max-rounds</span> <span class="s">10</span>
  <span class="r">:prompt</span> <span class="s">"Rewrite the homepage
  features section..."</span>)</pre>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-number">02</div>
      <h3>8 built-in tools</h3>
      <p>Every LLM step gets read_file, grep, search, symbols, run, eval, check, and index by default. Restrict to a subset or pass an empty list for legacy behavior.</p>
      <pre class="code feature-code"><span class="r">;; restrict to specific tools</span>
(<span class="k">llm</span> <span class="r">:tools</span> [<span class="s">"glitch_read_file"</span>
             <span class="s">"glitch_grep"</span>]
  <span class="r">:prompt</span> <span class="s">"Check what commands exist..."</span>)</pre>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-number">03</div>
      <h3>Tiered escalation</h3>
      <p>Start on your local model for free. gl1tch self-evaluates the output. Escalates to cloud only when quality demands it.</p>
      <pre class="code feature-code"><span class="r">;; tier 0: lm-studio (free)</span>
<span class="r">;; tier 1: copilot</span>
<span class="r">;; tier 2: claude</span>
(<span class="k">llm</span> <span class="r">:provider</span> <span class="s">"lmstudio"</span> <span class="r">:prompt</span> <span class="s">"..."</span>)</pre>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-number">04</div>
      <h3>S-expressions, not YAML</h3>
      <p>Workflows are parenthesized lists. Every construct composes — retry wraps timeout wraps step. No indentation wars. No anchor hacks.</p>
      <pre class="code feature-code">(<span class="k">retry</span> <span class="s">2</span>
  (<span class="k">with-timeout</span> <span class="s">30</span>
    (<span class="k">step</span> <span class="s">"fetch"</span>
      (<span class="k">sh</span> <span class="s">"curl -sf ..."</span>))))</pre>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-number">05</div>
      <h3>Phase gates</h3>
      <p>Verification built into the language. Gates must pass before the workflow continues. LLM-powered gates can use tools to verify claims against the codebase.</p>
      <pre class="code feature-code">(<span class="k">step</span> <span class="s">"gate"</span>
  (<span class="k">llm</span> <span class="r">:agentic</span> <span class="s">true</span>
    <span class="r">:prompt</span> <span class="s">"Verify no hallucinated
    commands. Return JSON..."</span>))</pre>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-number">06</div>
      <h3>Built-in A/B testing</h3>
      <p>Run the same prompt through different models or strategies. A neutral judge scores each branch. One form, automatic winner selection.</p>
      <pre class="code feature-code">(<span class="k">compare</span>
  (<span class="k">branch</span> <span class="s">"local"</span>
    (<span class="k">llm</span> <span class="r">:provider</span> <span class="s">"lmstudio"</span> <span class="r">:prompt</span> <span class="s">"..."</span>))
  (<span class="k">branch</span> <span class="s">"cloud"</span>
    (<span class="k">llm</span> <span class="r">:provider</span> <span class="s">"claude"</span> <span class="r">:prompt</span> <span class="s">"..."</span>))
  (<span class="k">review</span> <span class="r">:criteria</span> (<span class="s">"accuracy"</span> <span class="s">"clarity"</span>)))</pre>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-card">
      <div class="feature-number">07</div>
      <h3>Plugins are directories</h3>
      <p>A plugin is a folder of <code>.glitch</code> files. Each file is a subcommand. Args become flags. No compilation. No release pipeline.</p>
      <pre class="code feature-code"><span class="p">$</span> glitch plugin github prs --since week
<span class="r">["Fix flaky test", "Add retry logic"]</span></pre>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- ── The workflow ─────────────────────────── -->
<section id="how">
<div class="wrap-wide">
  <div class="section-label">how it works</div>
  <h2>The LLM pulls its own context. You write the intent.</h2>

  <div class="how-grid">
    <div class="how-step">
      <div class="how-num">01 shell gathers the seed</div>
      <pre class="code">(<span class="k">step</span> <span class="s">"pr"</span>
  (<span class="k">sh</span> <span class="s">"gh pr view ~input --json title,body,files"</span>))</pre>
      <p>Shell steps fetch what you already know you need — a PR number, a commit SHA, a file list. Fast and deterministic.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="how-step">
      <div class="how-num">02 LLM explores on demand</div>
      <pre class="code">(<span class="k">step</span> <span class="s">"review"</span>
  (<span class="k">llm</span> <span class="r">:agentic</span> <span class="s">true</span> <span class="r">:max-rounds</span> <span class="s">10</span>
    <span class="r">:prompt</span> <span class="s">"PR: ~(ref \"pr\")
    Read the changed files.
    Review as a senior engineer."</span>))</pre>
      <p>The LLM reads files, greps for usages, and checks symbols — looping until it has enough context. No pre-stuffing required.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="how-step">
      <div class="how-num">03 C.L.E.A.R. gates verify</div>
      <pre class="code">(<span class="k">step</span> <span class="s">"gate"</span>
  (<span class="k">llm</span> <span class="r">:agentic</span> <span class="s">true</span>
    <span class="r">:tools</span> [<span class="s">"glitch_read_file"</span> <span class="s">"glitch_grep"</span>]
    <span class="r">:prompt</span> <span class="s">"Verify against codebase.
    Return JSON: &#123;pass: bool, issues: [...]&#125;"</span>))</pre>
      <p>LLM-powered gates using C.L.E.A.R. — Clarity, Logic, Empathy, Actionability, Relevance. Agentic gates read the repo to verify claims.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="how-step">
      <div class="how-num">04 compare and pick the best</div>
      <pre class="code">(<span class="k">compare</span>
  (<span class="k">branch</span> <span class="s">"local"</span>
    (<span class="k">llm</span> <span class="r">:provider</span> <span class="s">"lmstudio"</span> <span class="r">:agentic</span> <span class="s">true</span>
      <span class="r">:prompt</span> <span class="s">"..."</span>))
  (<span class="k">branch</span> <span class="s">"cloud"</span>
    (<span class="k">llm</span> <span class="r">:provider</span> <span class="s">"claude"</span> <span class="r">:agentic</span> <span class="s">true</span>
      <span class="r">:prompt</span> <span class="s">"..."</span>))
  (<span class="k">review</span> <span class="r">:criteria</span> (<span class="s">"accuracy"</span> <span class="s">"depth"</span>)))</pre>
      <p>Run agentic branches in parallel, let a neutral judge score them. Pick the winner automatically.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- ── This site builds itself ─────────────── -->
<section id="meta">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="section-label">proof it works</div>
  <h2>This site builds itself.</h2>
  <p class="section-copy">Every page on this site was written by a gl1tch workflow. The LLM reads existing pages, greps the codebase for examples, and writes copy that matches what's actually true. C.L.E.A.R. gates verify every page before it hits disk.</p>

  <pre class="code meta-trace"><span class="p">$</span> glitch run site "update homepage"

<span class="term-header">&gt;&gt; site</span> <span class="term-anno">router</span>
  <span class="term-dim">&gt;</span> <span class="term-dim">pages</span>
  <span class="term-llm">&gt;</span> <span class="term-llm">route</span>                  <span class="term-anno">openrouter/gemma4</span>
  <span class="term-anno">&rarr; homepage</span>

<span class="term-header">&gt;&gt; site-homepage</span> <span class="term-anno">:agentic true</span>
  <span class="term-llm">&gt;</span> <span class="term-llm">rewrite</span>                <span class="term-anno">copilot</span>
  <span class="term-anno">  &rarr; glitch_read_file site/src/pages/index.astro</span>
  <span class="term-anno">  &rarr; glitch_read_file bb/src/glitch/core.clj</span>
  <span class="term-anno">  &rarr; glitch_read_file bb/src/glitch/mcp/tools.clj</span>
  <span class="term-anno">  &rarr; glitch_grep ":agentic" bb/providers/</span>
  <span class="term-llm">&check;</span> <span class="term-llm">rewrite</span>                <span class="term-anno">11586 chars &middot; 4 rounds</span>

<span class="term-header">&gt;&gt; site-homepage</span> <span class="term-anno">gate</span>
  <span class="term-llm">&gt;</span> <span class="term-llm">gate</span>                   <span class="term-anno">copilot :agentic true</span>
  <span class="term-anno">  &rarr; glitch_grep ":tools" bb/src/glitch/core.clj</span>
  <span class="term-anno">  &rarr; glitch_read_file bb/providers/copilot.clj</span>
  <span class="term-pass">&check;</span> <span class="term-gate">gate</span>                   <span class="term-pass">PASS</span> <span class="term-anno">no hallucinated features</span>

  <span class="term-dim">&gt;</span> <span class="term-dim">save</span>                   <span class="term-anno">site/src/pages/index.astro</span></pre>

  <div class="meta-suite">
    <div class="meta-cmd">
      <code>glitch run site "add a page about agentic steps"</code>
      <span>LLM reads the codebase, writes the page, C.L.E.A.R. gates verify, saves to disk</span>
    </div>
    <div class="meta-cmd">
      <code>glitch run site "update homepage"</code>
      <span>Agentic rewrite — LLM reads current page + source files, updates with verified content</span>
    </div>
    <div class="meta-cmd">
      <code>glitch run site "refresh all doc pages"</code>
      <span>Regenerate every page sequentially, each gated</span>
    </div>
    <div class="meta-cmd">
      <code>glitch run site "start dev server"</code>
      <span>Astro dev server with hot reload on port 4322</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- ── Agent integration ────────────────────��� -->
<section id="agents">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="section-label">integrations</div>
  <h2>Give your agents gl1tch.</h2>
  <p class="section-copy">gl1tch runs an MCP server that exposes 8 tools — read files, grep, search, run workflows, and more. Any MCP-compatible agent gets full access to your codebase through glitch.</p>

  <div class="agent-cards">
    <div class="agent-card">
      <div class="agent-card-label">Claude Code</div>
      <pre class="code copyable" data-copy="claude mcp add glitch -- glitch mcp"><span class="p">$</span> claude mcp add glitch -- glitch mcp</pre>
      <p>Adds glitch as an MCP server. Claude can read files, grep code, run workflows, and search your indexed repos — all from within a conversation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="agent-card">
      <div class="agent-card-label">Copilot CLI</div>
      <pre class="code copyable" data-copy="copilot --additional-mcp-config mcp.json"><span class="p">$</span> copilot --additional-mcp-config <span class="s">mcp.json</span></pre>
      <p>Point copilot at glitch's MCP config. It calls tools automatically — reads files, verifies facts, runs workflows mid-conversation.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="agent-card">
      <div class="agent-card-label">Any MCP client</div>
      <pre class="code copyable" data-copy="glitch mcp"><span class="p">$</span> glitch mcp</pre>
      <p>Starts a stdio MCP server. Pipe it into any MCP-compatible client — Cursor, Windsurf, custom agents. 8 tools: <code>read_file</code>, <code>grep</code>, <code>search</code>, <code>run</code>, <code>eval</code>, <code>check</code>, <code>symbols</code>, <code>index</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</section>

</main>

</Base>
